    "title": "Greetings from Kyiv, where you might stumble across Zelenskyy taking a stroll - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Nick Spicer ,\n14 days ago Far-Flung Postcards is a weekly series in which NPR's international team shares moments from their lives and work around the world. The Maidan, Kyiv's Independence Square, has been the heart of political change in Ukraine for more than two decades. While visiting NPR's team covering Ukraine — correspondent Joanna Kakissis and producers Hanna Palamarenko and Polina Lytvynova — I went back to the square, where history-making news events have drawn me for over two decades. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 3",
